    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33430" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλασ-τρέω</span></b> , 
			Ep.
		 and 
			Ion.
		 for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλαύνω, πολλοὶ δ᾽ ἀροτῆρες . .
			ζεύγεα δινεύοντες ἐλάστρεον</span> they <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>drove</i> the teams, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				18.543
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατ᾽ ἀμαξιτὸν ἣν ἠλάστρεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thgn.
					600
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. τινά</span>
			<i>to drive about</i>, of the Furies, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IT</u>
				971
			</span></i>; in later Prose, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαιμονίοις χόλοις ἐλαστρηθέντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					1.23
				</span></i>
			; <i>row</i>, 
				Ion.
			
			part.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλαστρεῦντας </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-εύοντας</span> codd.) <i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>Ind.</u>
				32.9
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, of ships, <i>to be rowed</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.158
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				7.24
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλαστροῦται</span>
				(sic)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">: ἐλαύνεται</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ιῶν: διαγινώσκων</span>,
		Id.</div>
